 the output weights are trained. Training involves adjusting the output weights to map the reservoir's activations to the desired output. Reservoirs in ESNs are often trained using random connectivity to capture complex dynamics, but the exact training process can vary.\n\nSummarizing the arXiv papers, none of the top results specifically mention echo state networks for anomaly detection. The closest matches are about graph neural networks and anomaly detection frameworks, not ESNs.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":1060,"prompt_eval_duration":44523000,"total_duration":2017483100}}